  "limitations": [
    "The source recordings retain original control-openhands playback timing, with no editorial speed change. CLI summary duration is rounded; exact container duration, frame count and capture counters are recorded for every original. Video is evidence of the control sequence, not a finer-grained timing instrument.",
    "Coverage is standalone Local Canvas in Neutral, Light+ and DeepSea at 1440×1000 desktop and 390×844 phone. No Cloud, ACP, all-five-theme or arbitrary embedded-host pass is claimed.",
    "Editorial labels and title cards are distinct from real app viewports. Actual UI pixels, including normal displayed temporary paths, are unretouched; public JSON omits local machine paths.",
    "Initial After captures with the expanded Getting started checklist are superseded. Final selected sources use the real UI to collapse the checklist before replay.",
    "The configured drawer and backdrop CSS duration is 0.25 s. Observer-visible hidden-but-mounted segments are sampled DOM presence after the actual timer has started; they are not exact elapsed mount intervals or measurements of every animation frame.",
    "Forced reduced-motion emulation is unavailable through the normal CLI. The captures record the actual reduced-motion preference as false. Source clips use the supported 25 fps maximum; early aborted attempts are excluded."
  ]
